      "round_summary": "Round 2/3: Fixed input_change_propagates_to_output_within_3 assertion in gray.scala, line 41. Root cause: `RegNext(io.i)` without a reset value gave `prev_i` a non-deterministic initial value (solver picks 1 at time 0 while io.i=0), causing a spurious `input_changed=true` that activated the bounded-liveness monitor despite no actual input change. Since the output never actually changed, the counter expired after 3 cycles and fired the assertion. Fix: Changed `RegNext(io.i)` to `RegNext(io.i, 0.B)` on line 41, giving `prev_i` a deterministic initial value of 0.B. This prevents the spurious monitor activation at time 0 because `io.i === prev_i` (both 0) when no input change has occurred. Error type: assertion_error (monitor setup issue, not DUT bug). Target assertion label `input_change_propagates_to_output_within_3` preserved exactly. No homologous assertions needed — the only other RegNext without reset is in the stable_cnt logic (line 73) which is structurally different (comparison direction is safe: mismatches reset the counter, preventing false assertions).",
